{"id":"mahabharata-6-094","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":94,"title":"चतुर्नवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 94 · Bhishma's reply and his refusal to kill Shikhandin","summary":{"en":"Stung by Duryodhana's harsh words, Bhishma answers sadly that no one can defeat the Pandavas, and promises to fight to the end. He declares he will not strike Shikhandin, who was born a woman.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಕಟುಮಾತಿನಿಂದ ನೊಂದ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಯಾರೂ ಗೆಲ್ಲಲಾರರೆಂದು ದುಃಖದಿಂದ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಕೊನೆಯವರೆಗೆ ಹೋರಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಭರವಸೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹೆಣ್ಣಾಗಿ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ಶಿಖಂಡಿಯನ್ನು ಹೊಡೆಯುವುದಿಲ್ಲ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन के कठोर शब्दों से आहत भीष्म दुःख से उत्तर देते हैं कि पाण्डवों को कोई नहीं जीत सकता और अन्त तक लड़ने का वचन देते हैं। वे कहते हैं कि स्त्री रूप में जन्मे शिखण्डी पर वे प्रहार नहीं करेंगे।","te":"దుర్యోధనుని కఠిన మాటలకు బాధపడిన భీష్ముడు పాండవులను ఎవరూ గెలవలేరని దుఃఖంతో బదులిచ్చి చివరి వరకు పోరాడతానని మాటిస్తాడు. స్త్రీగా పుట్టిన శిఖండిని తాను కొట్టనని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"துரியோதனனின் கடும் சொற்களால் புண்பட்ட பீஷ்மர் பாண்டவரை யாரும் வெல்ல முடியாது என்று துயரத்துடன் கூறி இறுதிவரை போரிடுவதாக உறுதியளிக்கிறார். பெண்ணாகப் பிறந்த சிகண்டியை அடிக்க மாட்டேன் என்று அறிவிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനന്റെ കടുത്ത വാക്കുകളാൽ മുറിവേറ്റ ഭീഷ്മർ, പാണ്ഡവരെ ആർക്കും തോൽപ്പിക്കാനാവില്ലെന്ന് ദുഃഖത്തോടെ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; അവസാനം വരെ പൊരുതുമെന്ന് വാക്കുനൽകുന്നു. സ്ത്രീയായി ജനിച്ച ശിഖണ്ഡിയെ താൻ പ്രഹരിക്കില്ലെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.94; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"वाक्शल्यैस्तव पुत्रेण सोऽतिविद्धः पितामहः ।\nदुःखेन महताविष्टो नोवाचाप्रियमण्वपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by your son's words like darts, the grandsire was seized with great grief, yet he did not say the slightest unkind thing."}},{"n":2,"text":"स ध्यात्वा सुचिरं कालं दुःखरोषसमन्वितः ।\nश्वसमानो यथा नागः प्रणुन्नो वै शलाकया ॥","meaning":{"en":"He brooded for a long while, full of sorrow and anger, and sighed like a snake that has been prodded with a stick."}},{"n":3,"text":"उद्वृत्य चक्षुषी कोपान्निर्दहन्निव भारत ।\nसदेवासुरगन्धर्वं लोकं लोकविदां वरः ।\nअब्रवीत्तव पुत्रं तु सामपूर्वमिदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rolling his eyes in rage, as though burning up the world with its gods, demons, and gandharvas, that best of those who know the world spoke to your son, first with soothing words."}},{"n":4,"text":"किं नु दुर्योधनैवं मां वाक्शल्यैरुपविध्यसि ।\nघटमानं यथाशक्ति कुर्वाणं च तव प्रियम् ।\nजुह्वानं समरे प्राणांस्तवैव हितकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana, why do you pierce me thus with the darts of your words, when I strive with all my strength to do what you like, and offer up my life in battle, wishing only your good?"}},{"n":5,"text":"यदा तु पाण्डवः शूरः खाण्डवेऽग्निमतर्पयत् ।\nपराजित्य रणे शक्रं पर्याप्तं तन्निदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the brave Pandava satisfied Agni at Khandava, having beaten Indra in the fight, that is proof enough."}},{"n":6,"text":"यदा च त्वां महाबाहो गन्धर्वैर्हृतमोजसा ।\nअमोचयत्पाण्डुसुतः पर्याप्तं तन्निदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the son of Pandu freed you, mighty-armed one, after the gandharvas had carried you off by force, that is proof enough."}},{"n":7,"text":"द्रवमाणेषु शूरेषु सोदरेषु तथाभिभो ।\nसूतपुत्रे च राधेये पर्याप्तं तन्निदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When your heroic brothers and Karna, the son of Radha, were running away, that is proof enough."}},{"n":8,"text":"यच्च नः सहितान्सर्वान्विराटनगरे तदा ।\nएक एव समुद्यातः पर्याप्तं तन्निदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When, at the city of Virata, he alone went against all of us together, that is proof enough."}},{"n":9,"text":"द्रोणं च युधि संरब्धं मां च निर्जित्य संयुगे ।\nकर्णं च त्वां च द्रौणिं च कृपं च सुमहारथम् ।\nवासांसि स समादत्त पर्याप्तं तन्निदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he defeated the furious Drona and me, and Karna, you, Drona's son, and the great chariot-fighter Kripa, and took away our garments, that is proof enough."}},{"n":10,"text":"निवातकवचान्युद्धे वासवेनापि दुर्जयान् ।\nजितवान्समरे पार्थः पर्याप्तं तन्निदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Partha conquered in battle the Nivatakavachas, who cannot be beaten even by Vasava, that is proof enough."}},{"n":11,"text":"को हि शक्तो रणे जेतुं पाण्डवं रभसं रणे ।\nत्वं तु मोहान्न जानीषे वाच्यावाच्यं सुयोधन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who can conquer in battle the furious Pandava? But you, Suyodhana, in your folly do not know what ought to be said and what not."}},{"n":12,"text":"मुमूर्षुर्हि नरः सर्वान्वृक्षान्पश्यति काञ्चनान् ।\nतथा त्वमपि गान्धारे विपरीतानि पश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man about to die sees all the trees as golden; so you, son of Gandhari, see everything reversed."}},{"n":13,"text":"स्वयं वैरं महत्कृत्वा पाण्डवैः सहसृञ्जयैः ।\nयुध्यस्व तानद्य रणे पश्यामः पुरुषो भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You yourself made this great enmity with the Pandavas and the Srinjayas. Fight them today, then; let us see you be a man."}},{"n":14,"text":"अहं तु सोमकान्सर्वान्सपाञ्चालान्समागतान् ।\nनिहनिष्ये नरव्याघ्र वर्जयित्वा शिखण्डिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As for me, tiger among men, I shall kill all the assembled Somakas and Panchalas, except Shikhandin."}},{"n":15,"text":"तैर्वाहं निहतः संख्ये गमिष्ये यमसादनम् ।\nतान्वा निहत्य संग्रामे प्रीतिं दास्यामि वै तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Either I shall be slain by them in battle and go to Yama's abode, or I shall kill them and so please you."}},{"n":16,"text":"पूर्वं हि स्त्री समुत्पन्ना शिखण्डी राजवेश्मनि ।\nवरदानात्पुमाञ्जातः सैषा वै स्त्री शिखण्डिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandin was born first as a woman in a king's house and became a man by a boon; that Shikhandin is truly a woman."}},{"n":17,"text":"तामहं न हनिष्यामि प्राणत्यागेऽपि भारत ।\nयासौ प्राङ्निर्मिता धात्रा सैषा वै स्त्री शिखण्डिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will not kill her, Bharata, even if it costs me my life. She who was first made a woman by the Creator is indeed a woman, Shikhandini."}},{"n":18,"text":"सुखं स्वपिहि गान्धारे श्वोऽस्मि कर्ता महारणम् ।\nयज्जनाः कथयिष्यन्ति यावत्स्थास्यति मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sleep well, son of Gandhari. Tomorrow I will fight a great battle, one that people will tell of as long as the earth endures.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तव सुतो निर्जगाम जनेश्वर ।\nअभिवाद्य गुरुं मूर्ध्ना प्रययौ स्वं निवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, your son, lord of the people, left; bowing his head to his elder, he went to his own dwelling."}},{"n":20,"text":"आगम्य तु ततो राजा विसृज्य च महाजनम् ।\nप्रविवेश ततस्तूर्णं क्षयं शत्रुक्षयंकरः ।\nप्रविष्टः स निशां तां च गमयामास पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arriving there, the king dismissed the great crowd, that destroyer of enemies, and quickly entered his own house; having entered, he passed that night there."}}]}]}